A||||6||DISenchanted||Just a few minor questions
Z||000000||DISenchanted||09-03-99||11:07 AM||||I have a few questions reguarding my 85gt that I could use some assistance with.  I recently bought the car for next to nothing.  Some kid was about to sell it to a salvage yard and I couldn't let it happen.  I'll start with what works on he car.  It drives.  <p>Now to what doesn't,  The fan has been rigged so that the "normal" button on the climate control turns it on.  The Air conditioning compressor has been yanked right out.  The Engine mount that the dog bone attaches to is broken.  The Drive line shock absorber is broken.  The hose from the Air filter is broken.  Etc...<p>What I need help with is,  <p>Question #1<br>My speedometer works sometimes, the rest of the time is sits at 20mph until I reach 50 or so.  Then the gauge jumps from 20 - 65.  Any ideas?<p>Question #2<br>The car occasionally stalls.  No perticular reason. Usually when warm.  She'll fire up, but if you don't give her gas right away she dies.  It isn't very often though.<p>Question #3<br>Can anyone tell me what error code  "_  .."  means?  Long on, long off, short on, short off, short on.<p>Qusetion #4<br>When driving down the road at night,(it's only happened at night.) the "check engine" light comes on.  I pull over and open the trunk.  Close it and the car is fine?<p>Other then that, the car has a few quirks.  I'm just happy she didn't get junked.<p>Thank you for your time,<p>Chad
Z||000001||Patrick||09-03-99||11:49 AM||||<br><b>One flash, pause, two flashes</b> is normal. This is a <b>code 12</b> which should repeat three times before any other code is displayed. If that's the only code that comes up, consider yourself fortunate.<p>
Z||000002||DISenchanted||09-03-99||12:04 PM||||Ok, I feel stupid.<p>Now it displays,<p>Short short short pause short short<p>And<p>Short short short pause short short short short short
Z||000003||Patrick||09-03-99||12:16 PM||||<br>The codes are numbered according to the number of flashes before and after the pause. Therefore:<p>Code 32 - EGR system (exhaust gas recirculation)<p>Code 35 - IAC valve (idle air control)<p><br>
Z||000004||theogre||09-03-99||01:03 PM||||the fan comes on anytine an AC funtion is on. It has nothing to do with the compressor.<p>Since the AC system was likely not plugged when the compressor was removed you likely have very expensive repairs to fix it. The hose to the compressor is no longer made. You'll have to fabricate at least that. You'll also need to flush the system, replace the ACC/dryer and orifice tube. You'll also need to test the system at full pressure with nitrogen to make sure the evaporator and condensor are still good.
Z||000005||AL||09-03-99||06:51 PM||||why don't you look at the junkyards for what you need, ask them to try to locate them for you.remember that if you fix it not only will you have a good car but you will feel good knowing you saved a future classic.  
Z||000006||GWMORGAN||09-03-99||07:50 PM||||I know of only one hose (two in one) which is made by AC DELCO. Cost...about $90 from retail parts store, over $140 from GM dealer. This hose runs from the AC compessor and connects just below the air filter housing.
